  "findings": [
    "The engine simple-cloud material supports stratocumulus, altostratus, cirrostratus and nimbostratus; its storm scalar does not construct a cumulonimbus tower/anvil.",
    "The dense native rain deck strongly darkens the alley. Histogram exposure favors the dark scene while the roughly 2.4% sky opening contributes little; rain also had an additional +0.6 EV bias.",
    "Exposure-only A/B reduces white sky luminance but does not produce the required storm-cell silhouette. Removing fog or bloom barely changes sky contrast.",
    "The accepted new material uses absolute cloud ray-sample world position, base/tower/anvil density envelopes, volume-noise erosion and physical wind drift. Clear weather blends back to the native graph."
  ],
